{"step_index":6276,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T01:16:02Z","thinking":"Analyzing the CSS, `.servers-grid` uses a grid layout, adjusting columns based on screen width. The `.server-detail-value` class focuses on styling text within server details, setting font and weight. The details text is being styled within that context.\n\n\nThe unbroken URL string within the server details was creating a fixed minimum width for each card, leading to horizontal overflow. Lack of `word-break` and `min-width: 0` in several CSS classes exacerbated this, preventing the layout from adapting to narrower screens.  Missing `overflow-x: hidden;` on the `body` and other layout elements allowed the horizontal scrollbar to appear.\n\n\nThe existing logging implementation sends server logs to the pipeline terminal. The user's request involves separating server management logs into a dedicated terminal. This necessitates modifying the logging callback to differentiate between pipeline and server logs.\n\nSuspect the `add_log` function currently dispatches all log messages to the pipeline. Changing the `logger_callback` passed to `MSEMAXServerManager` to use a different logging mechanism for server instance will ensure separate terminal outputs. Also, investigating server shutdown reliability is needed.\n\n\nInvestigating the `ServerInstance.stop()` method to understand server shutdown behavior and potential causes of port conflicts, particularly under Windows. The logic attempts to terminate the server process using `taskkill` or `os.killpg` depending on the operating system. It also attempts to identify and terminate orphaned processes still listening on the same port.\n\nAnalyzing the exception handling within `stop()`. The code includes an exception handler, however it merely logs the exception; it does not translate the generic exception into a user-friendly message, potentially leading to the display of raw error information. This may cause port conflicts. The `is_port_listening` function requires examination.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nimport socket\nfor port in [8000, 8001]:\n    with socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM) as s:\n        s.settimeout(0.5)\n        res = s.connect_ex(('127.0.0.1', port))\n        print(f'Port {port}:', 'LISTENING' if res == 0 else 'CLOSED')\n\"","Cwd":"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking port 8000 and 8001 status","toolSummary":"Check ports 8000 and 8001"}}]}
